{%- liquid
  # Live plan pricing from the Pro product. Variants resolve by SKU —
  # lifetime access is always SKU SL-PRO-LIFE, never a title match — with
  # static text and deep-link fallbacks when the product cannot resolve.
  assign pro_product = all_products['swinglab-pro']
  assign monthly_cents = 0
  assign season_cents = 0
  assign monthly_live = ''
  assign season_live = ''
  assign founders_live = ''
  assign coach_live = ''
  assign coach_yearly_live = ''
  assign season_permo_live = ''
  assign monthly_live_url = ''
  assign season_live_url = ''
  assign founders_live_url = ''
  assign coach_live_url = ''
  if pro_product != blank
    for variant in pro_product.variants
      if variant.sku == 'SL-PRO-LIFE'
        assign founders_live = variant.price | money
        assign founders_live_url = variant.url
      elsif variant.sku == 'SL-PRO-12MO'
        assign season_cents = variant.price
        assign season_live = variant.price | money
        assign season_permo_live = variant.price | divided_by: 12 | money
        assign season_live_url = variant.url
      elsif variant.sku == 'SL-PRO-1MO'
        assign monthly_cents = variant.price
        assign monthly_live = variant.price | money
        assign monthly_live_url = variant.url
      elsif variant.sku == 'SL-COACH-1MO'
        assign coach_live = variant.price | money
        assign coach_live_url = variant.url
      elsif variant.sku == 'SL-COACH-12MO'
        assign coach_yearly_live = variant.price | money
      endif
    endfor
    if monthly_live == ''
      assign monthly_cents = pro_product.price_min
      assign monthly_live = pro_product.price_min | money
    endif
  endif

  assign save_pct = 42
  if monthly_cents > 0 and season_cents > 0
    assign yearly_equiv = monthly_cents | times: 12
    if yearly_equiv > season_cents
      assign save_pct = yearly_equiv | minus: season_cents | times: 100.0 | divided_by: yearly_equiv | round
    endif
  endif

  # Split the blocks by type up front. The old markup walked section.blocks
  # twice and filtered inline, which meant the ladder's <ul> was emitted even
  # when it held nothing — on the new 1px-gap grid that is a visible empty
  # bordered box, not the harmless nothing it used to be. Filtering here also
  # lets forloop.index be the spec-sheet number directly, instead of a hand
  # -rolled counter that would otherwise start the ladder at 02.
  assign free_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'free_band'
  assign plan_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'plan'
-%}

<section id="{{ section.settings.anchor | default: 'plans' }}"
         class="sl-plans"{% if section.settings.membership_section %} data-app-upgrade-section{% endif %}>
  <div class="sl-wrap">
    {%- comment -%}
      Asymmetric, left-aligned, and split across two columns — the old head
      was a centred eyebrow/h2/lede stack, which was the shape every other
      band on the page also used. The rule underneath is the section's own
      structure rather than a decorative flourish.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <header class="sl-plans__head sl-reveal">
      <div class="sl-plans__head-lead">
        <p class="sl-eyebrow">{{ 'homepage.plans.eyebrow' | t }}</p>
        <h2 class="sl-plans__title">
          {%- if section.settings.membership_section -%}
            <span data-app-auth-signed-out>{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Start free. Go Pro when the reps matter.' }}</span>
            <span data-app-auth-signed-in hidden>{{ 'homepage.plans.member_heading' | t }}</span>
          {%- else -%}
            {{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Start free. Go Pro when the reps matter.' }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="sl-plans__head-note">
        {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
          <p class="sl-plans__sub"{% if section.settings.membership_section %} data-app-auth-signed-out{% endif %}>{{ section.settings.subheading }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.membership_section -%}
          <p class="sl-plans__sub" data-app-auth-signed-in hidden>{{ 'homepage.plans.member_subheading' | t }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </header>

    {%- comment -%}
      The free entry point leads. The old order rendered Free last, after
      all three paid tiers — the product's actual on-ramp buried under the
      things it upsells to.

      It is the sunk well (--sl-night) where the paid cards are raised
      panels, so the base unit reads as the floor of the ladder rather than
      as a fourth card that lost.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for block in free_blocks -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign fb = block.settings
        assign free_url = fb.url
        if free_url == blank
          assign free_url = 'https://app.caddieinsight.com/signup'
        endif
      -%}
      <aside class="sl-plans__free sl-reveal sl-reveal--d1"
             aria-labelledby="PlansFree-{{ section.id }}"
             {% if fb.member_visibility == 'signed_out' %}data-app-auth-signed-out{% endif %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
        {%- comment -%}
          Same webp ladder and the same candidate widths as the paid cards.
          The free band used to top out at 480w against a hard-coded
          sizes="148px", so the free tier's photograph could never resolve
          past a third of what the paid slots delivered, and the media box
          stayed pinned at 148px even once the band stacked and had the room.
          Its source photograph, caddieinsight-free-card-v2.png, stays in
          assets/ as the record behind the rungs but is no longer requested.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="sl-plans__free-media" aria-hidden="true">
          {%- if fb.image -%}
            <img
              src="{{ fb.image | image_url: width: 480 }}"
              srcset="{{ fb.image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ fb.image | image_url: width: 960 }} 960w, {{ fb.image | image_url: width: 1536 }} 1536w"
              sizes="(min-width: 560px) 200px, calc(100vw - 48px)"
              width="{{ fb.image.width }}"
              height="{{ fb.image.height }}"
              alt=""
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async">
          {%- else -%}
            <img
              src="{{ 'caddieinsight-free-card-v2-480.webp' | asset_url }}"
              srcset="{{ 'caddieinsight-free-card-v2-480.webp' | asset_url }} 480w, {{ 'caddieinsight-free-card-v2-960.webp' | asset_url }} 960w, {{ 'caddieinsight-free-card-v2-1536.webp' | asset_url }} 1536w"
              sizes="(min-width: 560px) 200px, calc(100vw - 48px)"
              width="1536"
              height="1024"
              alt=""
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async">
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="sl-plans__free-copy">
          <p class="sl-plans__rail">
            <span class="sl-plans__index">00</span>
            {%- if fb.note != blank -%}<span class="sl-plans__badge">{{ fb.note }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          </p>
          <h3 id="PlansFree-{{ section.id }}" class="sl-plans__free-name">{{ fb.name | default: 'CaddieInsight Free' }}</h3>
          {%- if fb.description != blank -%}<p class="sl-plans__free-desc">{{ fb.description }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <div class="sl-plans__free-side">
          <p class="sl-plans__free-price">{{ fb.price_text | default: '$0' }}</p>
          <a class="sl-btn sl-plans__cta sl-plans__ghost" href="{{ free_url }}">{{ fb.cta_label | default: 'Start free' }}</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- if plan_blocks.size > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        role="list" is not redundant here: Safari drops list semantics from a
        <ul> once list-style is none, and this one is also display: grid.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="sl-plans__grid sl-reveal sl-reveal--d2" role="list">
        {%- for block in plan_blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign b = block.settings
            # max_blocks caps this section at six blocks, so the ladder can
            # never reach 10 and one leading zero is always the right width.
            assign card_index = forloop.index | prepend: '0'

            assign plan_price = ''
            assign plan_permo = ''
            assign plan_yearly = ''
            assign plan_variant_url = ''
            assign plan_deeplink = ''
            assign plan_price_default = ''
            assign plan_permo_default = ''
            assign plan_yearly_default = ''
            if b.plan == 'season'
              assign plan_price = season_live
              assign plan_permo = season_permo_live
              assign plan_variant_url = season_live_url
              assign plan_deeplink = '/products/swinglab-pro?variant=46811170209964'
              assign plan_price_default = '$69.99'
              assign plan_permo_default = '$5.83'
            elsif b.plan == 'founders'
              assign plan_price = founders_live
              assign plan_variant_url = founders_live_url
              assign plan_deeplink = '/products/swinglab-pro?variant=46839745282220'
              assign plan_price_default = '$249'
            elsif b.plan == 'coach'
              assign plan_price = coach_live
              assign plan_yearly = coach_yearly_live
              assign plan_variant_url = coach_live_url
              assign plan_deeplink = '/products/swinglab-pro?variant=46906759741612'
              assign plan_price_default = '$19.99'
              assign plan_yearly_default = '$139.99'
            else
              assign plan_price = monthly_live
              assign plan_yearly = season_live
              assign plan_variant_url = monthly_live_url
              assign plan_deeplink = '/products/swinglab-pro?variant=46811170177196'
              assign plan_price_default = '$9.99'
              assign plan_yearly_default = '$69.99'
            endif

            # The author's "Price fallback" now outranks the packaged literal.
            # It used to be consulted only for monthly and founders — coach and
            # season jumped straight to a hard-coded string — so index.json
            # could carry price_text: "$19.99" and a correction typed there
            # would be silently ignored on exactly the day the live variant
            # stopped resolving, which is the only day the setting matters.
            if plan_price == blank
              assign plan_price = b.price_text
            endif
            if plan_price == blank
              assign plan_price = plan_price_default
            endif
            if plan_permo == blank
              assign plan_permo = plan_permo_default
            endif
            if plan_yearly == blank
              assign plan_yearly = plan_yearly_default
            endif

            assign plan_url = b.url
            if plan_url == blank
              assign plan_url = plan_variant_url
            endif
            if plan_url == blank
              assign plan_url = plan_deeplink
            endif

            # The saving is a property of paying yearly, so the chip belongs on
            # the line that quotes the yearly price. It used to render in the
            # price row too, which put "Save 42%" beside $9.99/mo — a claim the
            # monthly plan is the discount, i.e. exactly backwards.
            assign show_price_chip = false
            assign show_yearly_chip = false
            if b.show_save
              if b.plan == 'season'
                assign show_price_chip = true
              elsif plan_yearly != blank
                assign show_yearly_chip = true
              endif
            endif

            # Packaged card art ships as pre-encoded webp rungs (480/960/1536),
            # cut by store-assets/plan_card_webp.py. Theme webps must be served
            # whole via asset_url: asset_img_url is the legacy sizing filter,
            # it does not process webp, and it emits the no-image placeholder —
            # the same trap hero.liquid documents. So the responsive candidates
            # cannot be cut on the CDN and are baked instead. The source
            # photographs (caddieinsight-pro-card-v2.png and
            # caddieinsight-founders-card-v2.png) stay in assets/ as the record
            # behind them, but nothing here requests them: that was 3.7 MB of
            # uncompressed PNG on the section where someone decides to pay.
            # Every name is written out whole so theme-check's MissingAsset can
            # still verify the binding.
            #
            # These hold the FILENAME; asset_url is applied at each use site
            # below. Piping here instead reads better but trips theme-check's
            # RemoteAsset warning: it inspects the src attribute literally, and
            # a bare `{{ art_md }}` gives it no way to know the value already
            # went through asset_url, so it assumes a remote host. Newer
            # theme-check follows the assignment; the pinned 3.58.2 in CI does
            # not, and the workflow runs --fail-level warning.
            assign art_sm = 'caddieinsight-pro-card-v2-480.webp'
            assign art_md = 'caddieinsight-pro-card-v2-960.webp'
            assign art_lg = 'caddieinsight-pro-card-v2-1536.webp'
            # coach reuses the pro card art — same product family
            if b.plan == 'founders'
              assign art_sm = 'caddieinsight-founders-card-v2-480.webp'
              assign art_md = 'caddieinsight-founders-card-v2-960.webp'
              assign art_lg = 'caddieinsight-founders-card-v2-1536.webp'
            endif
          -%}
          <li class="sl-plans__card{% if b.featured %} sl-plans__card--featured{% endif %}"{{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <div class="sl-plans__media" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- if b.image -%}
                <img
                  src="{{ b.image | image_url: width: 960 }}"
                  srcset="{{ b.image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ b.image | image_url: width: 960 }} 960w, {{ b.image | image_url: width: 1536 }} 1536w"
                  sizes="(min-width: 1000px) 384px, min(100vw - 48px, 560px)"
                  width="{{ b.image.width }}"
                  height="{{ b.image.height }}"
                  alt=""
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async">
              {%- else -%}
                <img
                  src="{{ art_md | asset_url }}"
                  srcset="{{ art_sm | asset_url }} 480w, {{ art_md | asset_url }} 960w, {{ art_lg | asset_url }} 1536w"
                  sizes="(min-width: 1000px) 384px, min(100vw - 48px, 560px)"
                  width="1536"
                  height="1024"
                  alt=""
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async">
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
            <div class="sl-plans__card-body">
              <p class="sl-plans__rail">
                <span class="sl-plans__index">{{ card_index }}</span>
                {%- if b.badge != blank -%}<span class="sl-plans__badge">{{ b.badge }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              </p>
              <h3 class="sl-plans__name">{{ b.name | default: 'CaddieInsight Pro' }}</h3>
              <p class="sl-plans__price">
                <span class="sl-plans__amount">{{ plan_price }}</span>
                {%- if b.term != blank -%}<span class="sl-plans__term">{{ b.term }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                {%- if show_price_chip -%}<span class="sl-badge-save">{{ 'homepage.plans.save_chip' | t: percent: save_pct }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              </p>
              {%- if b.plan == 'season' -%}
                <p class="sl-plans__permo">{{ 'homepage.plans.permo' | t: amount: plan_permo }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if plan_yearly != blank -%}
                <p class="sl-plans__permo">{{ 'homepage.plans.yearly_line' | t: amount: plan_yearly }}{% if show_yearly_chip %} <span class="sl-badge-save">{{ 'homepage.plans.save_chip' | t: percent: save_pct }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if b.description != blank -%}<p class="sl-plans__desc">{{ b.description }}</p>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if b.note != blank -%}<p class="sl-plans__note">{{ b.note }}</p>{%- endif -%}
              <a class="sl-btn sl-plans__cta{% if b.featured %} sl-plans__cta--featured{% endif %}" href="{{ plan_url }}">{{ b.cta_label | default: 'Get Pro' }}</a>
            </div>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.footnote != blank -%}
      <p class="sl-plans__footnote">{{ section.settings.footnote }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* THIS SECTION CARRIES NO SIGNAL COLOUR, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN.
   Amber marks a value the engine measured; a price is an offer someone
   wrote, not a reading someone took, and a savings claim is merchandising.
   Cyan is the live read. Borrowing either here would cost them their
   meaning everywhere else on the page for a decorative gain, so the whole
   ladder is bone, hairline and mono. Emphasis is structural instead: the
   featured tier is raised and rule-capped, not coloured. */
.sl-plans {
  padding-top: var(--sl-section-space);
  padding-bottom: var(--sl-section-space);
  /* No panel of its own. body paints the 8px graph-paper field with
     background-attachment: fixed, so leaving this transparent lets the grid
     run under the ladder while the neighbours paint over it — these two
     rules are the whole separation, in place of another dark slab. */
  background: transparent;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
  color: var(--sl-ink);
}
/* The shared eyebrow is amber in base.css. On this section that would be
   the only amber, spent on a label — scoped back to a quiet mono line. */

.sl-plans__head {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--sl-space-5);
  padding-bottom: var(--sl-space-6);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  text-align: left;
}
.sl-plans__title {
  max-width: 20ch;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-heading-display);
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  line-height: 0.98;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
/* No display: rule here — the signed-in copy is toggled with [hidden] by
   sections/header.liquid, and any display value would defeat it. */
.sl-plans__sub {
  max-width: 46ch;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
  line-height: 1.55;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* ---- 00 · the base unit ---- */
.sl-plans__free {
  /* Below 1000px this shares the ladder's single 560px column. Left full
     width it spanned the viewport while the cards below it stayed capped,
     and the two read as two different systems on the same page. */
  margin: var(--sl-space-7) auto 0;
  max-width: 560px;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  align-items: stretch;
  /* The 1px-gap bordered grid: the container paints the hairline and each
     cell paints over it, so the seams are rules rather than gutters. */
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--sl-border);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
}
.sl-plans__free-media,
.sl-plans__free-copy,
.sl-plans__free-side { background: var(--sl-night); }
/* 200px, not the old 148px: the paid cards render their photograph at 384px,
   and at 148 the free tier's read as a contact sheet next to them rather than
   as the same campaign. It is still the compact band, just legible. */
.sl-plans__free-media {
  aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
  overflow: hidden;
  line-height: 0;
}
.sl-plans__free-media img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: center;
}
.sl-plans__free-copy { padding: var(--sl-card-inset); }
.sl-plans__free-name {
  margin: var(--sl-space-4) 0 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  line-height: 1.1;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-plans__free-desc {
  margin: var(--sl-space-3) 0 0;
  max-width: 58ch;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  line-height: 1.55;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.sl-plans__free-side {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: stretch;
  justify-content: flex-start;
  gap: var(--sl-space-4);
  padding: var(--sl-card-inset);
  text-align: left;
}
.sl-plans__free-price {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-2xl);
  font-weight: 500;
  line-height: 1;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* ---- the paid ladder ---- */
.sl-plans__grid {
  margin: var(--sl-space-7) auto 0;
  padding: 0;
  max-width: 560px;
  list-style: none;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  align-items: stretch;
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--sl-border);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
}
.sl-plans__card {
  position: relative;
  min-width: 0;
  height: 100%;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  background: var(--sl-bg);
  color: var(--sl-ink);
}
/* Every card carries the cap so the photographs stay on one baseline; only
   the featured one inks it. This used to be an amber gradient hairline —
   amber is a measured value on this system and a merchandising choice is
   not one, so the mark is bone, and the raised panel does the rest. */
.sl-plans__card::before {
  content: "";
  display: block;
  flex: none;
  height: 2px;
  background: transparent;
}
.sl-plans__card--featured {
  background: var(--sl-bg-card);
  box-shadow: var(--sl-shadow-card);
}
.sl-plans__card--featured::before { background: var(--sl-ink); }
.sl-plans__media {
  position: relative;
  aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
  overflow: hidden;
  line-height: 0;
  background: var(--sl-night);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
.sl-plans__media img {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: center;
  /* A touch of the range light out of it. The card renders are glossier
     than anything else on the field; this seats them without turning the
     thing you are buying into a grey plate. */
  filter: saturate(0.9) contrast(1.04) brightness(0.94);
}
/* the plate falls into the panel instead of ending on a hard edge */
.sl-plans__media::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(var(--sl-field-rgb), 0) 60%, rgba(var(--sl-field-rgb), 0.55) 100%);
}
.sl-plans__card-body {
  padding: var(--sl-card-inset);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: stretch;
  justify-content: flex-start;
  gap: var(--sl-space-2);
  flex: 1;
  text-align: left;
}
/* the spec-sheet rail: index in the margin, term beside it, rule under */
.sl-plans__rail {
  margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-2);
  padding-bottom: var(--sl-space-3);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--sl-space-3);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  line-height: 1;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-plans__index {
  padding: var(--sl-space-1) var(--sl-space-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
/* the second half of the featured mark — inverted, still bone */
.sl-plans__card--featured .sl-plans__index {
  border-color: var(--sl-ink);
  background: var(--sl-ink);
  color: var(--sl-bg);
}
.sl-plans__badge { margin: 0; }
.sl-plans__name {
  margin: var(--sl-space-2) 0 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  line-height: 1.1;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-plans__price {
  margin: var(--sl-space-2) 0 0;
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--sl-space-2) var(--sl-space-3);
}
/* Mono for every number on the surface, tabular so the three cards' prices
   line up down the ladder rather than drifting by digit width. */
.sl-plans__amount {
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-3xl);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  line-height: 1;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.sl-plans__term,
.sl-plans__permo {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
.sl-plans__term { text-transform: uppercase; }
/* base.css ships this chip as white on solid amber — 2.0:1, below AA, and
   amber spent on a marketing claim besides. Scoped here to a hairline mono
   tag that sits in the type rather than shouting over it. */
.sl-plans .sl-badge-save {
  padding: var(--sl-space-1) var(--sl-space-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.sl-plans__desc {
  margin: var(--sl-space-3) 0 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
  line-height: 1.55;
  flex: 1;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.sl-plans__note {
  margin: var(--sl-space-4) 0 0;
  padding-top: var(--sl-space-3);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  line-height: 1.5;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

/* ---- controls ----
   Scoped under .sl-plans because these override .sl-btn from base.css and
   the two sheets' load order is not this file's to guarantee. Bone on the
   field with a hairline edge, the same treatment as .sl-hero__primary —
   an amber button would read as a measured value. */
.sl-plans .sl-plans__cta {
  width: 100%;
  margin-top: var(--sl-space-4);
  min-height: 48px;
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-control-border);
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-control);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-weight: 600;
}
.sl-plans .sl-plans__cta:hover {
  border-color: var(--sl-ink);
  background: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.06);
  color: var(--sl-ink);
}
/* One filled button on the section. Bone fill, field-coloured label. */
.sl-plans .sl-plans__cta--featured {
  border-color: var(--sl-ink);
  background: var(--sl-ink);
  color: var(--sl-bg);
}
.sl-plans .sl-plans__cta--featured:hover {
  border-color: var(--sl-ink);
  background: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.88);
  color: var(--sl-bg);
}
/* The free band's cell is a flex column with its own gap, so the card
   button's stacking margin would double the space above it. */
.sl-plans .sl-plans__ghost { margin-top: 0; }

.sl-plans__footnote {
  margin: var(--sl-space-6) 0 0;
  padding-top: var(--sl-space-4);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  line-height: 1.6;
  text-align: left;
}

/* The buttons are deliberately absent here: .sl-btn already declares its own
   transition in base.css, and re-declaring it at this specificity would drop
   transform from the list and make base.css's gated hover lift snap. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .sl-plans__card { transition: background-color 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease; }
}
/* Hover lifts the panel, not the geometry: a translate would tear the 1px
   seams the grid is built from. */
.sl-plans__card:hover { background: var(--sl-bg-card); }
.sl-plans__card--featured:hover {
  background: var(--sl-bg-card);
  box-shadow: var(--sl-shadow-card-hover);
}

@media (min-width: 560px) {
  .sl-plans__free { grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .sl-plans__free-side { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
}
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-plans__head {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    gap: var(--sl-space-7);
    align-items: end;
  }
  .sl-plans__free {
    margin-inline: 0;
    max-width: none;
    grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(200px, 15rem);
  }
  .sl-plans__free-side {
    grid-column: auto;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .sl-plans__grid {
    margin-inline: 0;
    max-width: none;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }
}
/* No mobile reorder. The featured card used to be pulled to the top of the
   stack because an amber hairline was the only thing marking it and a
   visitor could scroll past it; it now carries a bone cap, a raised panel,
   an inverted index and the one filled button, so it does not need to jump
   the queue. Reordering also cost two things this layout depends on: the
   spec-sheet numbers ran 02, 01, 03, and the price ladder read $19.99,
   $9.99, $249 — block_order in templates/index.json is deliberate, and
   this is the one viewport that used to ignore it. */
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
